dt-bindings: gpu: mali-midgard: add mediatek,mt6797-mali

Track 2 (GPU/panfrost) staging, UNPROVEN — gemini_linux tracker #7.

The MT6797 (Helio X20/X27) integrates a Midgard-class Mali. Add a binding
entry so the Gemini PDA GPU node validates under dtbs_check: SoC compatible
"mediatek,mt6797-mali" with the generic "arm,mali-t880" fallback (already in
the panfrost of_match table, and already present here as a commented
placeholder — this promotes it to a real, matchable const).

Model choice, FLAGGED FOR OWNER REVIEW: our project notes call this a
Mali-T880 MP4, but the vendor 3.18 DTS (ubports-3.18
arch/arm64/boot/dts/mt6797.dts, node mali@13040000) labels the GPU
"arm,malit860"/"arm,mali-t86x". Panfrost identifies the actual GPU at runtime
from the GPU_ID register, so the fallback string is used only for driver
match + this schema check, never for capability; the T880-vs-T860 die is
immaterial to probe and unconfirmed without reading the part on hardware. We
use arm,mali-t880 per the project's stated target; arm,mali-t860 is the
vendor-DTS-consistent alternative (both resolve to panfrost default_data).

Signed-off-by: mratan <mattdratan@gmail.com>

